    faqKicker:'GOOD TO KNOW',faqHeading:'A few more questions?',faqIntro:'This is where “warranty” starts to feel less complicated.',faq1q:'Is a legal guarantee the same as a commercial warranty?',faq1a:'No. The legal guarantee comes from the law and usually binds the seller. A commercial warranty is an additional promise from a manufacturer or seller; it does not remove statutory rights.',faq2q:'Can I always ask for an immediate refund?',faq2a:'No. Repair or replacement often comes first, with exceptions for serious non-conformity or unsuccessful or refused remedies. Greece also has a special route for defects appearing within 30 days, subject to conditions.',faq3q:'Does the new law automatically add another year?',faq3a:'Not to every purchase. The new protection is linked to choosing repair under the legal guarantee. Greece provides a three-year limitation period for movable goods when repair is chosen, but not for sale contracts concluded before 31 July 2026.',faq4q:'Does the new repair right mean free manufacturer repairs?',faq4a:'No. It applies to specific categories where product-specific EU repairability requirements are applicable. Manufacturers may need to repair free or at a reasonable price. The model, affected part and relevant support period must be checked.',faq5q:'What about second-hand goods or buying from a private seller?',faq5a:'Second-hand goods bought from traders are also protected. Some countries allow an expressly agreed shorter guarantee of at least one year. Purely private sales do not receive the EU minimum legal guarantee for trader purchases.',faq6q:'Does the tool send my information anywhere?',faq6a:'Your answers and letters are processed on-device, without accounts, analytics or case-data APIs. The case is stored in your browser only if you choose Save locally. Like other websites, the hosting provider may record basic request details (such as IP addresses). Email is handed off to your own email app.',
